Pretest
1. A transmission line is mainly used to:
A. Store electrical energy
B. Transfer electromagnetic energy from source to load
C. Increase voltage only
D. Convert AC to DC
Answer: B
2. The speed of an electromagnetic wave depends primarily on:
A. Resistance only
B. Permittivity and permeability of the medium
C. Current only
D. Voltage only
Answer: B
3. Which material is commonly used as a dielectric in transmission lines?
A. Copper
B. Air, PTFE, or FR-4
C. Iron
D. Aluminum
Answer: B
4. Which parameter increases with increasing frequency in microwave circuits?
A. Wavelength decreases
B. Wavelength increases
C. Resistance becomes zero
D. Velocity becomes infinite
Answer: A
5. A stripline is classified as a:
A. Lumped-element circuit
B. Transmission line
C. DC circuit
D. Power supply
Answer: B
